cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lightsmith in your work, please cite it as below, and also cite the solver backends you used (see `lightsmith backends` and `Result.provenance`)."
type: software
title: "Lightsmith: an open, GPU-native, differentiable photonics suite for humans and AI agents"
abstract: >-
  Lightsmith describes a photonics problem once, as typed JSON, and solves it
  with Mie, T-matrix, BEM, DDA, FDTD, TMM, RCWA, FDE, EME, BPM, FDFD, PWE and
  S-matrix circuit solvers on CPU or GPU, with differentiable inverse design. Every
  result uses the same units and conventions and carries provenance, so methods
  can be cross-checked directly. Python, CLI and MCP interfaces are JSON in,
  JSON out.
authors:
  - family-names: Feghali
    given-names: Alexander
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lightsmith-photonics/lightsmith"
url: "https://docs.lightsmith.dev/"
keywords:
  - photonics
  - nanophotonics
  - electromagnetics
  - scattering
  - Mie theory
  - discrete dipole approximation
  - FDTD
  - RCWA
  - inverse design
  - GPU
